The two failed runs were stopped at 15 minutes while `racket/tests/rule-diff-test.rkt` was running. In my run that test started at the 13-minute mark, which fits a run cut off by the limit rather than a deadlock.

**The cause:** `ralph_loops/loop0003/knobs.json` had `gate_timeout_min: 15`. That's shorter than the gate whenever `racket/` changes, because the Python suite alone takes almost 11 minutes. Earlier gates fit because they ran only the Python suite.

**The fix:** I set `gate_timeout_min` back to 30, the driver's default, and added a note to `ralph_loops/loop0003/PROGRESS.md`. I didn't touch any test, golden trace, fixture, Chez file or Python engine module. Nothing was committed or pushed.

**Decision for you:** the git history shows the knob was lowered from 30 to 15 on purpose. If you want to keep 15 minutes, the test suites would have to get faster, because the gate can't finish in 15 minutes when `racket/` changes.

